@multidsh/dsh-webui-auth README · Known limits：- **The desktop app does not go through the password gate (since 0.3.6)**: the desktop renderer's requests are forwarded by the shell proxy, which stores no session cookies (it drops `set-cookie`), and a custom-scheme page has no usable cookie jar — so the desktop can only enter through the host-direct channel and cannot "log in inside the desktop". By design this is equivalent to "the desktop already holds the host launch token", the same trust boundary as "a local process can read the data directory"; the password gate guards the browser line (`dsh web`, LAN, reverse proxy).
- **The host-direct exemption is loopback-only**: a non-loopback client is still asked for the password even if it holds a core cookie or knows the launch token (the document gate only passes the token exchange, never the core-admitted predicate). Local reverse proxies (caddy/cloudflared) and SSH tunnels also look loopback to the Host and cannot be told apart from the desktop app, but such visitors are already inside the machine's trust boundary (they can read the session tokens in the data directory).
